{"tool_name":"neighbor-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"neighbor-seq","home":"https://github.com/sjdlabgroup/Neighborseq","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Reconstructing physical cell interaction networks from single-cell data using Neighbor-seq.","addition_date":"2022-08-27T11:29:06.288895Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:46:48.245737Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:neighbor-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"subhajyoti.de@rutgers.edu","name":"Subhajyoti De","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2313-8593","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Bassel Ghaddar"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"Neighbor-seq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkac333","metadata":{"abstract":"Cell-cell interactions are the fundamental building blocks of tissue organization and multicellular life. We developed Neighbor-seq, a method to identify and annotate the architecture of direct cell-cell interactions and relevant ligand-receptor signaling from the undissociated cell fractions in massively parallel single cell sequencing data. Neighbor-seq accurately identifies microanatomical features of diverse tissue types such as the small intestinal epithelium, terminal respiratory tract, and splenic white pulp. It also captures the differing topologies of cancer-immune-stromal cell communications in pancreatic and skin tumors, which are consistent with the patterns observed in spatial transcriptomic data. Neighbor-seq is fast and scalable. It draws inferences from 